{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature","id":367717,"title":"Spirit Sapience diverges from nature.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-12T12:38:24-08:00","id":367717,"title":"Spirit Sapience diverges from nature.","content":"Since past a certain point, spirits are sapient, doesn't that imply that once one has gotten powerful enough to rise above the equivalent of subsistence farming, they might start branching out from their nature and doing things because they enjoy them even if they don't generate food/power/Essence.<br /> <br /> For instance a spirit of murder that enjoys vegging out and watching TV. Or composing orchestras. Or keeping a very minor non-sapient spirit of glass as a pet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:45:59-08:00","id":367737,"title":"","content":"They kinda <i>can't</i>.<br /> <br /> It's like asking why people, if they're sapient, don't grow extra limbs, or speak a language they've never heard before. It's not impossible to imagine doing it, but you still can't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T12:46:01-08:00","id":367739,"title":"","content":"Spirits branch out by killing other spirits and grafting their thinking-about-other-stuff parts into their own nature. The ability to conceive of things outside the scope of their base purview is largely a function of an expanded conceptual palate rather than any inclination toward purposeless behavior on their part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:03:21-08:00","id":367752,"title":"","content":"They also expand their own sense of self over time if they become more powerful. An eagle spirit may start as a bird of prey, but over time it may take on aspects of freedom, or other things that might be symbolized with an eagle. A spirit of darkness may come to develop an influence of fear, or ignorance, or stealth and any number of things. And so more powerful spirits (higher ranked ones) tend to have a variety of influences and are often unique, or at least seem to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2015, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:26:20-08:00","id":367777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367739#post367739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits branch out by killing other spirits and grafting their thinking-about-other-stuff parts into their own nature. The ability to conceive of things outside the scope of their base purview is largely a function of an expanded conceptual palate rather than any inclination toward purposeless behavior on their part.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367752#post367752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also expand their own sense of self over time if they become more powerful. An eagle spirit may start as a bird of prey, but over time it may take on aspects of freedom, or other things that might be symbolized with an eagle. A spirit of darkness may come to develop an influence of fear, or ignorance, or stealth and any number of things. And so more powerful spirits (higher ranked ones) tend to have a variety of influences and are often unique, or at least seem to be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the expanded sense of self comes from the aforementioned killing and grafting. The eagle spirit starts as a bird of prey, then goes to places where the Resonant condition for it exists. Let's say it's an Eagles Nest right next to the highway. Tourists take photos there or pose with it because of the patriotic symbolism. They in turn create resonance for spirits of freedom or patriotism, which said eagle spirit may hunt and kill, consuming them and integrating their resonances until it becomes a more complicated spirit that mixes its influences and becomes Eagle Patriot or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:33:58-08:00","id":367785,"title":"","content":"It also comes from the essence of loci and from actions or non-actions across the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lareath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature#post367717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since past a certain point, spirits are sapient, doesn't that imply that once one has gotten powerful enough to rise above the equivalent of subsistence farming, they might start branching out from their nature and doing things because they enjoy them even if they don't generate food/power/Essence.<br /> <br /> For instance a spirit of murder that enjoys vegging out and watching TV. Or composing orchestras. Or keeping a very minor non-sapient spirit of glass as a pet.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can expand upon their nature naturally, but they can't go against their nature without becoming a magath. A murder spirit eating a sloth spirit, or hanging around a concert hall too much.<br /> <br /> It's all detailed in The Nature of Things, in the first chapter of the Predators book, on pages 14 and 15.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:48:06-08:00","id":367801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367785#post367785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also comes from the essence of loci and from actions across the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026Which themselves form tiny mindless spirits around them in the form of motes with some minuscule capacity for thought about [concept] Essence.<br /> <br /> Sheer weight of numbers means even a relatively &quot;pure&quot; spirit is going to eventually develop the ability to contemplate things conceptually related to its basis, whereupon the pressures of spiritual evolution may eventually cause it to adopt a neighboring aspect and in turn see <i>that</i> concept's related phenomena as of concern to it, and so on.<br /> <br /> It's still going to be a particularly alien being, seeing as its agenda and sense of self is bound up in being, say, a spirit of computers, airplanes, and bees. A diversification of limited modes of thought is still going to result in a limited mode of thought, if only in the sense that developing assets too far outside of that structure is a recipe for metaphysical insanity and ostracism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:08:29-08:00","id":367828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367801#post367801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u2026Which themselves form tiny mindless spirits around them in the form of motes with some minuscule capacity for thought about [concept] Essence.<br /> <br /> Sheer weight of numbers means even a relatively &quot;pure&quot; spirit is going to eventually develop the ability to contemplate things conceptually related to its basis, whereupon the pressures of spiritual evolution may eventually cause it to adopt a neighboring aspect and in turn see <i>that</i> concept's related phenomena as of concern to it, and so on.<br /> <br /> It's still going to be a particularly alien being, seeing as its agenda and sense of self is bound up in being, say, a spirit of computers, airplanes, and bees. A diversification of limited modes of thought is still going to result in a limited mode of thought, if only in the sense that developing assets too far outside of that structure is a recipe for metaphysical insanity and ostracism.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like a Spirit with a diverse conceptual spirit might give one the appearance of sentience based upon its ability to conceive of and think about a diversity of concepts, but that it's still more mimicking sentience than an actual example of it. Kinda like how they say there are Artificial Intelligences which pass the Turing Test. They're not really living intelligences, but they're sophisticated enough that they can fool you into thinking they are one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:15:35-08:00","id":367832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367828#post367828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds like a Spirit with a diverse conceptual spirit might give one the appearance of sentience based upon its ability to conceive of and think about a diversity of concepts, but that it's still more mimicking sentience than an actual example of it. Kinda like how they say there are Artificial Intelligences which pass the Turing Test. They're not really living intelligences, but they're sophisticated enough that they can fool you into thinking they are one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. It's an unbelievably complex occult entity, but it's still proscribed in its thought processes and incapable of considering things outside the context of their relation to itself and its nature. The Keeper of the Dead &quot;thinking it loves someone&quot; is a prime example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:01:12-08:00","id":368135,"title":"","content":"That being said, there are a few way in which you might meet a more well rounded spirit, but hardly common.<br /> <br /> The idigam can put souls into spirits, as well as vice versa, according to the rockies book, so a werewolf might encounter say a fire elemental that used to be an accountant who really enjoyed monday night football.<br /> , <br /> If a spirit eats a ghost, the resulting magath will retain more personality according to the UK book.<br /> <br /> And while it's rare, occasionally a human can become a spirit instead of a ghost, one example being the &quot;angels&quot; of a legacy from one of the legacy books, I don't recall the book mentioning anything about those &quot;angels&quot; becoming as monomaniacal as a regular spirit, although that could happen I suppose.<br /> <br /> I've suggested the idea of a numina along the lines of lucid dead from mummy for spirits, for example as such beings as mentioned above, and other non typical spirits. For example, in Bleeding Edge, AIs are computer spirits. An AI researcher makes an AI modelled off of human thought, but the result never ends with an AI that can think like a human? That's a little odd. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T19:13:50-08:00","id":368148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=368135#post368135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a spirit eats a ghost, the resulting magath will retain more personality according to the UK book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that ghosts taste awful and the spirits that do so tend to be related to death, the dead, or local beliefs about souls and ghosts very definitely get less humanlike with age and isolation from humanity even if they're not stuck inside the elemental complex of a denizen of Shadow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while it's rare, occasionally a human can become a spirit instead of a ghost, one example being the &quot;angels&quot; of a legacy from one of the legacy books, I don't recall the book mentioning anything about those &quot;angels&quot; becoming as monomaniacal as a regular spirit, although that could happen I suppose. </div> </div> </div>That's liches. They're a core-covered antagonist bloc in 2e and the Scions of God tend to keep quiet about the effects of their last Attainment for the very reason of its stigma.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, in Bleeding Edge, AIs are computer spirits. An AI researcher makes an AI modelled off of human thought, but the result never ends with an AI that can think like a human? That's a little odd. </div> </div> </div>The general package of human-things spirits aren't capable of has individual exceptions in the natures of spirits for which it makes sense. You'll recall human-spirits aren't a thing, that one of the example characters for Promethean 2e that we've been given used to be a chatbot, and that the horror-mystery-setting nature of the nWoD is such that if it's capable of acting like a human it's either borrowing/stealing/imitating qualities from a person or it's not actually an inhuman being (or else it's going to go horribly wrong somewhere down the line when an exception trips that wouldn't in a genuine human).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T11:47:20-08:00","id":369928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367828#post367828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like a Spirit with a diverse conceptual spirit might give one the appearance of sentience based upon its ability to conceive of and think about a diversity of concepts, but that it's still more mimicking sentience than an actual example of it. Kinda like how they say there are Artificial Intelligences which pass the Turing Test. They're not really living intelligences, but they're sophisticated enough that they can fool you into thinking they are one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's opening a much bigger can of worms, but I would point out that it's hard to come up with a definition of &quot;intelligence&quot; or &quot;sapience&quot; that disqualifies that sort of thing. If something is indistinguishable from a conscious mind to all outward appearance, it's hard to really say it's not one. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T12:21:04-08:00","id":369985,"title":"","content":"That's a good point.<br /> <br /> They're certainly more one dimensional than humans, but they have less concerns for survival due to being effectively immortal as long as they keep getting essence and don't get assimilated. They develop their own personalities, and names, they appreciate risk and are willing to take chances or we wouldn't have ridden and claimed. They're able to form their own opinions or we wouldn't have totems, they have their own memories, but 'tainted' by the memories of similar spirits. The perceived mindlessness of spirits seems less accurate as you go up the ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-14-2015, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T15:41:02-08:00","id":370223,"title":"","content":"The big thing with spirits is that they lack free will. They're slaves to their urges and bans,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:01:45-08:00","id":370247,"title":"","content":"The same way we're slave to our biological urges and knowledge of things that can kill us?<br /> <br /> If we got all of our mental and physical needs sated by the presence fire, and weren't hurt by it but could die from a lack of it, wouldn't we all be pyromaniacs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-14-2015, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T16:12:15-08:00","id":370272,"title":"","content":"No. Not at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T17:04:33-08:00","id":370355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=369928#post369928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's opening a much bigger can of worms, but I would point out that it's hard to come up with a definition of &quot;intelligence&quot; or &quot;sapience&quot; that disqualifies that sort of thing. If something is indistinguishable from a conscious mind to all outward appearance, it's hard to really say it's not one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'm totally aware. I think it's one of those fun things to ship around and might be cause for interesting discussion among characters aware of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=370247#post370247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same way we're slave to our biological urges and knowledge of things that can kill us?<br /> <br /> If we got all of our mental and physical needs sated by the presence fire, and weren't hurt by it but could die from a lack of it, wouldn't we all be pyromaniacs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the point is that the stuff that composes a spirit's &quot;Alien Mindset&quot; is just how single-mindedly they can pursue essence. Even the most byzantine of plots that a higher ranked Spirit can initiate is still in service of that urge to create and consume Essence. It's how a Spirit of Joy can go bad, to go to that classic example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T18:00:22-08:00","id":370475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=370355#post370355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point is that the stuff that composes a spirit's &quot;Alien Mindset&quot; is just how single-mindedly they can pursue essence. Even the most byzantine of plots that a higher ranked Spirit can initiate is still in service of that urge to create and consume Essence. It's how a Spirit of Joy can go bad, to go to that classic example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the problem with spirits is that they really don't have empathy for the abstract or social consciences. They may care about others in their group if they're spirits of social animals, they may care about helping solve negative emotions if they're spirits of their opposites (or maybe therapy-spirits) but spirits don't have much beyond that, nor do they understand &quot;selflessness&quot; or &quot;self-destructiveness&quot; except academically, hence their lacking of Virtues and Vices. <br /> <br /> Thus, they never really internalize the idea of becoming more than they are, because they can't appreciate the idea that they <i>can </i>be, except as <i>magath </i>(which is almost always bad for the spirit, and they know that). Unless they're Immundi (spirits corrupted by the Inferno in the form of the Maeljin), and then they simply don't care (because they are fundamentally spirits of a self-centered and self-destructive concept, then). That's why they can be such problems to humans; they don't get why they shouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T05:54:27-08:00","id":370912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [b]Satchel: Spirits branch out by killing other spirits and grafting their thinking-about-other-stuff parts into their own nature. The ability to conceive of things outside the scope of their base purview is largely a function of an expanded conceptual palate rather than any inclination toward purposeless behavior on their part. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I tend to conceive of the Shadow Realm as a plane of ideas more than anything else. Spirits are living concepts - they become broader by becoming less pure, diluted with the essence of another concept, be it from a spirit or from human activity - or they remain pure and stuck in the rut of only ever being that one thing, hopelessly obsessive by human standards - or get stronger by eating a spirit of their own kind, much like ideas get set harder in your head by reinforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T05:55:00-08:00","id":370913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Satchel:</b> Spirits branch out by killing other spirits and grafting their thinking-about-other-stuff parts into their own nature. The ability to conceive of things outside the scope of their base purview is largely a function of an expanded conceptual palate rather than any inclination toward purposeless behavior on their part. </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I tend to conceive of the Shadow Realm as a plane of ideas more than anything else. Spirits are living concepts - they become broader by becoming less pure, diluted with the essence of another concept, be it from a spirit or from human activity - or they remain pure and stuck in the rut of only ever being that one thing, hopelessly obsessive by human standards - or get stronger by eating a spirit of their own kind, much like ideas get set harder in your head by reinforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:14:31-08:00","id":370916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=367832#post367832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right. It's an unbelievably complex occult entity, but it's still proscribed in its thought processes and incapable of considering things outside the context of their relation to itself and its nature. The Keeper of the Dead &quot;thinking it loves someone&quot; is a prime example.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Keeper of the Drowned in Last Rites was a deliberate exploration on my part of how the more powerful and individual spirits approach things like emotions, planning and ambitions, albeit a lot of it is via inference and implication given the short story is from the point of view of the werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T05:29:44-08:00","id":372216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=370913#post370913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I tend to conceive of the Shadow Realm as a plane of ideas more than anything else. Spirits are living concepts - they become broader by becoming less pure, diluted with the essence of another concept, be it from a spirit or from human activity - or they remain pure and stuck in the rut of only ever being that one thing, hopelessly obsessive by human standards - or get stronger by eating a spirit of their own kind, much like ideas get set harder in your head by reinforcement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Spirits are more than reflections of mere ideas. Fire isn't just an idea. Neither is pain. Nor is it grief. Food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:29:06-07:00","id":434992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=369985#post369985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point.<br /> <br /> They're certainly more one dimensional than humans, but they have less concerns for survival due to being effectively immortal as long as they keep getting essence and don't get assimilated. They develop their own personalities, and names, they appreciate risk and are willing to take chances or we wouldn't have ridden and claimed. They're able to form their own opinions or we wouldn't have totems, they have their own memories, but 'tainted' by the memories of similar spirits. The perceived mindlessness of spirits seems less accurate as you go up the ranks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Furthermore, there are spirits that will ride or merge with humans just for the enjoyment of wearing flesh, so there's more to it than some are suggesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T10:19:39-07:00","id":435889,"title":"","content":"I would purpose that Spirits have a form of Sapience but not one as we would categorize scientifically or comparatively.<br /> <br /> To be direct, I would purpose that Spirits are living narratives, ones that are aware of their origins, their existence in the scheme of other narratives and their future.<br /> <br /> A better way to conceptualize it might be that of a human actor playing a part in a play, they know why they are in that play, what role they have and what they must do, otherwise the whole play falls apart into chaos and loses its narrative. This loss presents weakness to other plays, or other actors who want their part. Spirits are predators after all and will subsume lesser parts in this play, <b>taking on their roles in the process</b>, and the whole play will change until it finds an equilibrium again where most of the time its the same thing over and over again with minor variations.<br /> <br /> Plays are subjective however, so some could be classical, others could be very new age, and that depends on the Spirit choir.<br /> <br /> How does this factor into Spirit Sapience?<br /> <br /> They are aware they are actors, but they must act. They understand where your coming from if you talk to them, but why are you not saying your lines properly? What role are you playing? Spirits can't figure humans or Uratha out for the most part because our roles are fluid and ever changing. Spirits have their own goals and motivations, like humans do, but their all centered on their role in the play.<br /> <br /> They want to make Romeo live. Or a king. Or actually secretly in love with Mercutio. They have plans for their role man. Big plans. Lesser spirits can't see past their roles and just enact them, greater spirits are aware of their roll and have ambitions or decisions about it. Gods among spirits are the deus ex machina of plays, so far removed they can alter them on a whim. They're kings and queens who commission certain plays because they fancy it. They are unknowable.<br /> <br /> That's how I frame the alien spirit sapience. Their stuck in their roles, but can see around them, they want things like we want things, but for the benefit of their roll and their continued existence in the grand play of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Oh, and they also want to kill and eat each other battle royal style (mostly) while they do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","user":"GilboD","date":". 03-10-2015, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T13:38:06-07:00","id":436137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilboD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367717-spirit-sapience-diverges-from-nature?p=435889#post435889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would purpose that Spirits have a form of Sapience but not one as we would categorize scientifically or comparatively.<br /> <br /> To be direct, I would purpose that Spirits are living narratives, ones that are aware of their origins, their existence in the scheme of other narratives and their future.<br /> <br /> A better way to conceptualize it might be that of a human actor playing a part in a play, they know why they are in that play, what role they have and what they must do, otherwise the whole play falls apart into chaos and loses its narrative. This loss presents weakness to other plays, or other actors who want their part. Spirits are predators after all and will subsume lesser parts in this play, <b>taking on their roles in the process</b>, and the whole play will change until it finds an equilibrium again where most of the time its the same thing over and over again with minor variations.<br /> <br /> Plays are subjective however, so some could be classical, others could be very new age, and that depends on the Spirit choir.<br /> <br /> How does this factor into Spirit Sapience?<br /> <br /> They are aware they are actors, but they must act. They understand where your coming from if you talk to them, but why are you not saying your lines properly? What role are you playing? Spirits can't figure humans or Uratha out for the most part because our roles are fluid and ever changing. Spirits have their own goals and motivations, like humans do, but their all centered on their role in the play.<br /> <br /> They want to make Romeo live. Or a king. Or actually secretly in love with Mercutio. They have plans for their role man. Big plans. Lesser spirits can't see past their roles and just enact them, greater spirits are aware of their roll and have ambitions or decisions about it. Gods among spirits are the deus ex machina of plays, so far removed they can alter them on a whim. They're kings and queens who commission certain plays because they fancy it. They are unknowable.<br /> <br /> That's how I frame the alien spirit sapience. Their stuck in their roles, but can see around them, they want things like we want things, but for the benefit of their roll and their continued existence in the grand play of the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Oh, and they also want to kill and eat each other battle royal style (mostly) while they do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like the True Fae to me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3642-lareath","name":"Lareath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:19:55-07:00","id":436334,"title":"","content":"They're honestly not super crazy different.<br /> <br /> ....Except for the fact that Spirits are part of a whole, where as True Fae are a whole and its parts, and that True Fae have no originality. Spirits have no limits on their creativity beyond their nature and role in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> The whole example was meant to frame Spirits in context we humans can relate to and describe how they view the world saliently. They're a lot more primal and predatory then they are shakespear but they are defined by their natures, their &quot;roles'', and can't compare or relate to things beyond their scope.<br /> <br /> They can shape their natures as they get stronger, direct them, and even become aware of the world beyond but they can't ever stop being their nature, their role to play in Shadow.<br /> <br /> The wolf must hunt, the banker must hoard, the crow must scavenge, the gun must shoot, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> It's how they see the world and how they act within it, always centered around what they must do, because they are Spirits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4134-gilbod","name":"GilboD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}